<title>MEXICO: Acer buys Brazilian firm for $13.2 mln.</title>
<headline>Acer buys Brazilian firm for $13.2 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Acer Computec Latino America SA de CV (ACLA), a Mexican maker and distributor of computers, announced on Monday it had purchased ACBr do Brasil, a subsidiary of ACLA do Brasil, for $13.2 million.</p>
<p>The sales price included the rights to distribute Acer products in Brazil, a company statement said.</p>
<p>The purchase will be partly financed from an initial public offering undertaken last year.</p>
<p>ACBr do Brasil is based in Sao Paulo and currently has an installed capacity of 70,000 units per year.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9552))</p>
